<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 01-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 01-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Marie, with 75 mph winds, is in the open waters of the western Pacific near 30n/170e, moving northeast at 25 mph. This system will become extratropical over the next 24-30 hours as it continues to accelerate northeastward. The threat to shipping posed by this system will gradually diminish this period.  </p>
<p>There are no other statements at this time.</p>
</text>
